; Specification: 3GPP TS 29.154
; Version: 19.0.0
; Vendor-ID: 10415
; Bases: RFC6733
; Link: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/129100_129199/129154/19.00.00_60/ts_129154v190000p.pdf


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#btr-request-asp-identity)
; AVP: Application-Service-Provider-Identity
; Command: BT-Request
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 9
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Based on the SCS/AS request, the SCEF shall send the Background-Data-Transfer-Request (BTR) command to the PCRF including the Transfer-Request-Type AVP with the value TRANSFER_POLICY_REQUEST(0), it shall also include the ASP identifier within the Application-Service-Provider-Identity AVP, volume of data per UE within the CC-Output-Octets AVP for downlink volume and/or the CC-Input-Octets AVP for uplink volume, or the CC-Total-Octets AVP for total volume regardless direction, expected number of UEs within the Number-Of-UEs AVP and desired time window within the Time-Window AVP."
    present-if Transfer-Request-Type = 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#btr-request-volume)
; AVP: CC-Total-Octets
; Command: BT-Request
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 9
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Based on the SCS/AS request, the SCEF shall send the Background-Data-Transfer-Request (BTR) command to the PCRF including the Transfer-Request-Type AVP with the value TRANSFER_POLICY_REQUEST(0), it shall also include the ASP identifier within the Application-Service-Provider-Identity AVP, volume of data per UE within the CC-Output-Octets AVP for downlink volume and/or the CC-Input-Octets AVP for uplink volume, or the CC-Total-Octets AVP for total volume regardless direction, expected number of UEs within the Number-Of-UEs AVP and desired time window within the Time-Window AVP."
    present-if Transfer-Request-Type = 0 and not CC-Output-Octets and not CC-Input-Octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#btr-request-number-of-ues)
; AVP: Number-Of-UEs
; Command: BT-Request
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 9
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Based on the SCS/AS request, the SCEF shall send the Background-Data-Transfer-Request (BTR) command to the PCRF including the Transfer-Request-Type AVP with the value TRANSFER_POLICY_REQUEST(0), it shall also include the ASP identifier within the Application-Service-Provider-Identity AVP, volume of data per UE within the CC-Output-Octets AVP for downlink volume and/or the CC-Input-Octets AVP for uplink volume, or the CC-Total-Octets AVP for total volume regardless direction, expected number of UEs within the Number-Of-UEs AVP and desired time window within the Time-Window AVP."
    present-if Transfer-Request-Type = 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#btr-request-time-window)
; AVP: Time-Window
; Command: BT-Request
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 9
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Based on the SCS/AS request, the SCEF shall send the Background-Data-Transfer-Request (BTR) command to the PCRF including the Transfer-Request-Type AVP with the value TRANSFER_POLICY_REQUEST(0), it shall also include the ASP identifier within the Application-Service-Provider-Identity AVP, volume of data per UE within the CC-Output-Octets AVP for downlink volume and/or the CC-Input-Octets AVP for uplink volume, or the CC-Total-Octets AVP for total volume regardless direction, expected number of UEs within the Number-Of-UEs AVP and desired time window within the Time-Window AVP."
    present-if Transfer-Request-Type = 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#bta-request-transfer-policy)
; AVP: Transfer-Policy
; Command: BT-Answer
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 9
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"When all existing transfer policies are retrieved, the PCRF shall determine one or more transfer policies based on the information received from the SCEF and other available information (e.g. network policy, congestion level (if available), load status estimation for the required time window and network area, existing transfer policies) and respond with a Background-Data-Transfer-Answer (BTA) command including the possible transfer policies within Transfer-Policy AVP (s) and a reference ID within Reference-Id AVP."
    present-if request/Transfer-Request-Type = 0 and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS
"The Transfer-Policy AVP(s) shall include the Transfer-Policy-Id AVP, the Time-Window AVP, the Rating-Group AVP, and may also include an Max-Requested-Bandwidth-DL AVP and/or an Max-Requested-Bandwidth-UL AVP."
    members at-least-one Time-Window
    members at-least-one Rating-Group


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#bta-request-reference-id)
; AVP: Reference-Id
; Command: BT-Answer
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 9
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"When all existing transfer policies are retrieved, the PCRF shall determine one or more transfer policies based on the information received from the SCEF and other available information (e.g. network policy, congestion level (if available), load status estimation for the required time window and network area, existing transfer policies) and respond with a Background-Data-Transfer-Answer (BTA) command including the possible transfer policies within Transfer-Policy AVP (s) and a reference ID within Reference-Id AVP."
    present-if request/Transfer-Request-Type = 0 and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#bta-pcrf-address)
; AVP: PCRF-Address
; Command: BT-Answer
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 9
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If more than one transfer policies are included in the BTA command, the PCRF shall also include the PCRF Id within the PCRF-Address AVP in the BTA command."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#btr-notification-reference-id)
; AVP: Reference-Id
; Command: BT-Request
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 9
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If there is more than one transfer policy provided from the PCRF to the SCEF in the BTA command, when the SCEF receives the selected transfer policy from the SCS/AS, the SCEF shall send Background-Data-Transfer-Request (BTR) command to the PCRF including the Transfer-Request-Type AVP set to the value TRANSFER_POLICY_NOTIFICATION (1)."
"The SCEF shall also include the reference ID in the Reference-Id AVP, the identity of the selected transfer policy within the Transfer-Policy-Id AVP and the destination PCRF Id within the Destination-Host AVP."
    present-if Transfer-Request-Type = 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#btr-notification-transfer-policy-id)
; AVP: Transfer-Policy-Id
; Command: BT-Request
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 9
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If there is more than one transfer policy provided from the PCRF to the SCEF in the BTA command, when the SCEF receives the selected transfer policy from the SCS/AS, the SCEF shall send Background-Data-Transfer-Request (BTR) command to the PCRF including the Transfer-Request-Type AVP set to the value TRANSFER_POLICY_NOTIFICATION (1)."
"The SCEF shall also include the reference ID in the Reference-Id AVP, the identity of the selected transfer policy within the Transfer-Policy-Id AVP and the destination PCRF Id within the Destination-Host AVP."
    present-if Transfer-Request-Type = 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#btr-notification-destination-host)
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Command: BT-Request
; Section: 4.4.1
; Page: 9
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If there is more than one transfer policy provided from the PCRF to the SCEF in the BTA command, when the SCEF receives the selected transfer policy from the SCS/AS, the SCEF shall send Background-Data-Transfer-Request (BTR) command to the PCRF including the Transfer-Request-Type AVP set to the value TRANSFER_POLICY_NOTIFICATION (1)."
"The SCEF shall also include the reference ID in the Reference-Id AVP, the identity of the selected transfer policy within the Transfer-Policy-Id AVP and the destination PCRF Id within the Destination-Host AVP."
    present-if Transfer-Request-Type = 1


; Type: Application Scope
; Name: Nt
; Section: 5.1
; Page: 10
; Application-ID: 16777348
; Applies-To: 5.*


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#btr-auth-session-state)
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: BT-Request
; Section: 5.2
; Page: 10
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"In order to indicate that the session state is not to be maintained, the Diameter client and server shall include the Auth-Session-State AVP with the value set to NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), in the request and in the answer messages (see IETF RFC 6733 [15])."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#bta-auth-session-state)
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: BT-Answer
; Section: 5.2
; Page: 10
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"In order to indicate that the session state is not to be maintained, the Diameter client and server shall include the Auth-Session-State AVP with the value set to NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), in the request and in the answer messages (see IETF RFC 6733 [15])."
    range 1


; Type: Application Scope
; Name: Nta
; Section: A.6.1
; Application-ID: 16777358
; Applies-To: A.6.*


; Type: Message
; Name: BT-Request, BTR
; Section: 5.6.2
; Page: 15
<BT-Request> ::= < Diameter Header: 8388723, REQ, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        [ DRMP ]
        { Vendor-Specific-Application-Id }
        { Auth-Session-State }
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        { Destination-Realm }
        { Transfer-Request-Type }
        [ Destination-Host ]
        [ OC-Supported-Features ]                 ; bold
        [ Application-Service-Provider-Identity ]
        [ CC-Output-Octets ]
        [ CC-Input-Octets ]
        [ CC-Total-Octets ]
        [ Number-Of-UEs ]
        [ Time-Window ]
        [ Network-Area-Info-List ]
        [ Reference-Id ]
        [ Transfer-Policy-Id ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ Route-Record ]
      * [ Supported-Features ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Message
; Name: BT-Answer, BTA
; Section: 5.6.3
; Page: 15
<BT-Answer> ::= < Diameter Header: 8388723, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        [ DRMP ]
        { Vendor-Specific-Application-Id }
        { Auth-Session-State }
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        [ Result-Code ]
        [ Experimental-Result ]
        [ Error-Message ]
        [ Error-Reporting-Host ]
        [ Failed-AVP ]
      * [ Redirect-Host ]
        [ Redirect-Host-Usage ]
        [ Redirect-Max-Cache-Time ]
        [ Reference-Id ]
        [ OC-Supported-Features ]          ; bold
        [ OC-OLR ]                         ; bold
      * [ Transfer-Policy ]
        [ PCRF-Address ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ Route-Record ]
      * [ Supported-Features ]
      * [ Load ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Message
; Name: EC-Request, ECR
; Section: A.6.6.2
<EC-Request> ::= < Diameter Header: 8388735, REQ, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        [ DRMP ]
        { Auth-Session-State }
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        { Destination-Realm }
        [ Destination-Host ]
        [ OC-Supported-Features ]       ; bold
        { External-Group-Identifier }
        [ Event-Configuration ]
        [ Group-Reporting-Guard-Timer ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ Route-Record ]
      * [ Supported-Features ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Message
; Name: EC-Answer, ECA
; Section: A.6.6.3
<EC-Answer> ::= < Diameter Header: 8388735, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        [ DRMP ]
        { Auth-Session-State }
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        [ Result-Code ]
        [ Experimental-Result ]
        [ Error-Message ]
        [ Error-Reporting-Host ]
        [ Failed-AVP ]
      * [ Redirect-Host ]
        [ Redirect-Host-Usage ]
        [ Redirect-Max-Cache-Time ]
        [ OC-Supported-Features ]      ; bold
        [ OC-OLR ]                     ; bold
        [ Event-Reports ]
        [ Event-Configuration-Status ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ Route-Record ]
      * [ Supported-Features ]
      * [ Load ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Message
; Name: ER-Request, ERR
; Section: A.6.6.4
<ER-Request> ::= < Diameter Header: 8388736, REQ, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        [ DRMP ]
        { Auth-Session-State }
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        { Destination-Realm }
        { Destination-Host }
        [ OC-Supported-Features ] ; bold
        [ Event-Reports ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ Route-Record ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Message
; Name: ER-Answer, ERA
; Section: A.6.6.5
<ER-Answer> ::= < Diameter Header: 8388736, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        [ DRMP ]
        { Auth-Session-State }
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        [ Result-Code ]
        [ Experimental-Result ]
        [ Error-Message ]
        [ Error-Reporting-Host ]
        [ Failed-AVP ]
      * [ Redirect-Host ]
        [ Redirect-Host-Usage ]
        [ Redirect-Max-Cache-Time ]
        [ OC-Supported-Features ]   ; bold
        [ OC-OLR ]                  ; bold
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ Route-Record ]
      * [ Load ]
      * [ AVP ]


