; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#transfer-policy-id-unique)
; AVP: Transfer-Policy-Id
; Within: Transfer-Policy
; Section: 5.3.9
; Page: 12
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"It is assigned by the PCRF and is unique per Reference-Id."
    unique


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#btr-supported-features-vendor)
; AVP: Supported-Features
; Command: BT-Request
; Section: 5.4.2
; Page: 13
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"On the all reference points as specified in this specification, the Supported-Features AVP is used to identify features that have been defined by 3GPP and hence, for features defined in this document, the Vendor-Id AVP shall contain the vendor ID of 3GPP (10415)."
    requires Supported-Features/Vendor-Id = 10415
"The Supported-Features AVP shall be included in every BTR and BTA commands if supported by the SCEF and PCRF respectively."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#bta-supported-features-vendor)
; AVP: Supported-Features
; Command: BT-Answer
; Section: 5.4.2
; Page: 13
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"On the all reference points as specified in this specification, the Supported-Features AVP is used to identify features that have been defined by 3GPP and hence, for features defined in this document, the Vendor-Id AVP shall contain the vendor ID of 3GPP (10415)."
    requires Supported-Features/Vendor-Id = 10415
"The Supported-Features AVP shall be included in every BTR and BTA commands if supported by the SCEF and PCRF respectively."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#btr-application-id)
; AVP: Vendor-Specific-Application-Id
; Command: BT-Request
; Section: 5.6.1
; Page: 14
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Nt application identifier shall be included in the Auth-Application-Id AVP within the Vendor-Specific-Application-Id grouped AVP contained in the BT-Request/Answer commands."
    requires Vendor-Specific-Application-Id/Auth-Application-Id = 16777348


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#bta-application-id)
; AVP: Vendor-Specific-Application-Id
; Command: BT-Answer
; Section: 5.6.1
; Page: 14
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Nt application identifier shall be included in the Auth-Application-Id AVP within the Vendor-Specific-Application-Id grouped AVP contained in the BT-Request/Answer commands."
    requires Vendor-Specific-Application-Id/Auth-Application-Id = 16777348


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#ecr-event-configuration)
; AVP: Event-Configuration
; Command: EC-Request
; Section: A.4.1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Based on the SCS/AS request to retrieve the location information for a group of UEs, the SCEF shall send an Event-Configuration-Request (ECR) command to the PCRF including the Event-Configuration AVP and the External-Group-Identifier AVP."
    text-only
"The Event-Configuration AVP shall include Monitoring-Type AVP with the value LOCATION_REPORTING (2), SCEF-ID AVP, Extended-SCEF-Reference-ID AVP and MONTE-Location-Type AVP within Location-Information-Configuration AVP."
    members at-least-one Location-Information-Configuration


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#event-configuration-location-reporting)
; AVP: Monitoring-Type
; Within: Event-Configuration
; Section: A.4.1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Event-Configuration AVP shall include Monitoring-Type AVP with the value LOCATION_REPORTING (2), SCEF-ID AVP, Extended-SCEF-Reference-ID AVP and MONTE-Location-Type AVP within Location-Information-Configuration AVP."
    range 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#event-configuration-monte-location-type)
; AVP: Location-Information-Configuration
; Within: Event-Configuration
; Section: A.4.1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Event-Configuration AVP shall include Monitoring-Type AVP with the value LOCATION_REPORTING (2), SCEF-ID AVP, Extended-SCEF-Reference-ID AVP and MONTE-Location-Type AVP within Location-Information-Configuration AVP."
    members at-least-one MONTE-Location-Type


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#eca-event-configuration-status)
; AVP: Event-Configuration-Status
; Command: EC-Answer
; Section: A.4.1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Once the PCRF receives the ECR command, the PCRF shall retrieve UE identities (MSISDN and optionally UE external identifier) for all UEs in the group associated with the External-Group-Identifier AVP from the SPR and respond with an Event-Configuration-Answer (ECA) command including the Event-Configuration-Status AVP."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#eca-final-report)
; AVP: Event-Configuration-State
; Within: Event-Configuration-Status
; Section: A.4.1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If the PCRF has at least one active IP-CAN session for received UE identities and for such IP-CAN session the PCEF/BBERF supports the NetLoc feature as defined in clause 5.4.1 of 3GPP TS 29.212 [aa], the Event-Configuration-State AVP within the Event-Configuration-Status AVP shall indicate this is not a final report with bit 0 not set."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#eca-netloc-not-supported)
; AVP: Event-Reports
; Command: EC-Answer
; Section: A.4.1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"For those UEs having active IP-CAN sessions but without the support of the NetLoc feature in the PCEF/BBERF, the PCRF shall also send Event-Reports AVP with NetLoc-Access-Support AVP set to the value NETLOC_ACCESS_NOT_SUPPORTED (0)."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#err-event-reports)
; AVP: Event-Reports
; Command: ER-Request
; Section: A.4.2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Event-Reports AVP shall include Extended-SCEF-Reference-ID AVP and the following information for each UE: MSISDN AVP or External-Identifier AVP (if available and local policy allows it) and Access-Network-Reports AVP (if available)."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#err-netloc-access-support)
; AVP: NetLoc-Access-Support
; Within: Access-Network-Reports
; Section: A.4.2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If the PCRF receives NetLoc-Access-Support AVP with the value NETLOC_ACCESS_NOT_SUPPORTED (0) from the PCEF/BBERF, it shall relay such AVP to the SCEF within the Access-Network-Reports AVP."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.154.dadx#ecr-auth-session-state)
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: EC-Request
; Section: A.6.2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"In order to indicate that the session state is not to be maintained, the Diameter client and server shall include the Auth-Session-State AVP with the value set to NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), in the request and in the answer messages (see IETF RFC 6733 [15])."
    range 1


